---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro'
import Prose from '~/components/Prose.astro'

// The privacy policy on Google's consent screen. Keep it in step with what
// convex/schema.ts stores.
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Tian stores, and where">
  <Prose>
    <h1>Privacy in Tian</h1>
    <p>
      Tian is a set of games for learning Mandarin, made by Gorm Rødder for
      family and friends. It has no advertising, no tracking and no analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>Without signing in</h2>
    <p>
      Your word bank, scores and settings are kept only in the browser on the
      device you use. None of it is sent to us, unless you turn on the daily
      reminder. The chat sends what it needs to Google, under your own key
      (below).
    </p>
    <h2>The chat</h2>
    <p>
      The chat is spoken by Google&rsquo;s Gemini, on an API key of your own
      that you paste into it. Signed out, the key is kept only in that
      browser. Signed in, it is kept on your account instead, encrypted with a
      secret that is not stored with it, so that it works on every device you
      sign in on; we use it only to ask Google for a token for each call you
      start, and it is never shown or sent back to the browser. Removing it in
      the chat deletes it.
    </p>
    <p>
      During a chat your browser sends to Google directly what you say into
      the microphone or type, and the words of your word bank, so that the
      conversation keeps to them. Google&rsquo;s terms for the Gemini API
      apply to that. None of it passes through us, and we keep none of it.
    </p>
    <h2>When you sign in with Google</h2>
    <p>We then store:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        your name, email address and profile picture from Google, to know who
        is signed in;
      </li>
      <li>
        your word bank: the words you have met, your scores and progress;
      </li>
      <li>
        if you keep it there, your Gemini API key for the chat, encrypted
        (above).
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We use this only to show you your progress on the devices where you are
      signed in, and the key only to start your chats. Gorm sees the names and email addresses of everyone who has
      signed in, and the first time you sign in, your name and email address
      are sent as a notification to Gorm's inbox on
      <a href="https://admin.ymse.land">admin.ymse.land</a>, which is also kept with
      Convex. We share nothing with anyone and use it for nothing else.
    </p>

    <h2>Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      What you write in the feedback form at the foot of the page, with the
      picture and the name or address you give with it, is sent to Gorm's inbox on
      <a href="https://admin.ymse.land">admin.ymse.land</a> and kept there,
      with Convex, until he deletes it. Tian itself keeps only when it was
      sent, for a day, to hold back floods.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
    <p>
      With <a href="https://www.convex.dev">Convex</a>, which runs the
      database for us on servers in Northern Virginia, USA. The sign-in itself
      goes through Google. The page loads its fonts from Google Fonts and the
      stroke order of characters from jsDelivr, which, like any website, see
      your IP address.
    </p>

    <h2>Deletion</h2>
    <p>
      If you want your account and everything that belongs to it deleted,
      write to <a href="mailto:gorm@ymse.land">gorm@ymse.land</a>, and we will
      delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:gorm@ymse.land">gorm@ymse.land</a>.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/about">About Tian</a></p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
